From 289521176f130d3e4b4005ade761a4cef40b39c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:00:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Optional libraries of MFEM: one option per library

Each library of MFEM which mfem-mgis uses for its solvers and
preconditioners has its own option, enable-<name>: AUTO by default (the
library is used if MFEM is built with it), ON (the library is required,
the configuration fails if MFEM is not built with it) or OFF (the library
is not used, even if MFEM is built with it). Libraries: petsc, ginkgo,
mumps, superlu, strumpack, suitesparse, sundials, mkl-pardiso,
mkl-cpardiso, cudss, magma (cmake/modules/MFEMMGISOptionalLibraries.cmake).

The sources, the headers and the tests use the macros
MFEM_MGIS_HAVE_<NAME>, public compile definitions of the target MFEMMGIS,
instead of the macros MFEM_USE_<NAME> of MFEM; the installed CMake
configuration gives the variables MFEMMGIS_HAVE_<NAME>. A package manager
can map each library to one switch, for instance the variants +petsc and
~petsc of a Spack package.

The messages refusing a solver or a preconditioner of an unavailable
library name its option (enable-<name>), and so do the messages refusing
the nonlinear solvers KINSOL and SNES. The option enable-magma selects the
sparse solvers of MAGMA only: the batched dense algebra of MFEM uses MAGMA
whenever MFEM is built with it.

Checked: the usual configuration (AUTO) builds the library and the tests;
with all the libraries OFF (MFEM of mmm-solvers, which has them all), the
library and the tests build, and the 238 tests pass.
